# C2 gate walk (tools/check_fixture_equivalence.sh, inc-10v7f): a human priest
# of The Multitude who takes the Inherent Spell feat, SAVED at the end of
# creation with nothing played. It exists to hit inherent_spell: a level-1
# priest is offered the feat (Observed in the feat menu, 2026-11-08) and then
# the "Choose an inherent spell" menu, which the walk answers by name. Point buy
# keeps the rolled sets and their perks out of the character. The two domain
# menus offer names the stream decides, so they take the first entry offered,
# the one choice here that is not by name.
a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
@choose "Human"
@choose "Athletics"
@choose "Diplomacy"
@choose "Priest"
@choose "The Multitude"
p       # Attributes: abort to Point Buy
RIGHT*6 DOWN RIGHT*8 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*4 DOWN RIGHT*8 DOWN RIGHT*9
ENTER   # every point spent
y       # Are these your final stats? -- yes
@choose "Neutral Evil"
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@choose "Alertness"
@choose "Inherent Spell"
@choose "Bless"
@choose "Dodge"
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN   # spend every rank
@while "Unspent Skill Ranks" ENTER y   # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
@while "Unspent Skill Ranks" ENTER y
@choose "The Ambitious Conqueror"
@expect "Learn Spells: Level"    # the starting-spells checklist
UP SPACE UP SPACE UP SPACE UP SPACE UP SPACE UP SPACE UP SPACE UP SPACE UP SPACE UP SPACE
ENTER
@while "Learn Spells: Level" ENTER
@until "System Menu" ESC
@expect "System Menu"
b       # [b] Save and Continue
@dump:saved
